\subsection{Phase I: Broad Performance Assessment}

This phase evaluates the overall system capability across diverse scenarios. A total of 71 queries were designed, distributed as follows:
\begin{itemize}
	\item \textbf{Productive Parcels (FR and PA):} 5 queries per parcel, focused on irrigation, fertilization, pest management, and investment ROI.
	\item \textbf{Non-Productive Parcels (UN and FO):} 4 queries per parcel, consisting of 2 functional queries and 2 \textit{Negative Testing Queries} (scenarios where the system must identify unsuitability).
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Phase II: Ablation Study (Architecture Validation)}

To quantify the impact and marginal contribution of each architectural module, an ablation study was conducted using a \textbf{factorial design}. Ablation studies consist of the individual analysis of different subsets (configurations) of a system, obtained through systematic activation and deactivation of its components. In this case, with three modules (Ortofoto, Satellite, and RAG, previously shown in \figref{fig:arch}), the factorial design of experiments yields $2^3 = 8$ possible configurations.

\begin{itemize}
	\item \textbf{Configurations:} 8 modular combinations + 1 Zero-Shot baseline (the LLM without parcel context) = 9 total configurations, listed in \tabref{tab:ablation_configs}.
	\item \textbf{Sample subset:} 1 representative parcel per Land Use category.
	\item \textbf{Query volume:} 2 specific queries per parcel across the 9 configurations $= \mathbf{72 \text{ queries}}$.
\end{itemize}

